# 7. ServiceAccount Tokens

A Pod that needs to authenticate to the Kubernetes API requires credentials.

Modern Kubernetes commonly uses **short-lived, automatically rotated ServiceAccount tokens** that are projected into Pods.

A projected token can be available inside the container at:

```text
/var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/
```

Commonly available files include:

```text
ca.crt
namespace
token
```

The exact behavior can depend on Pod and cluster configuration.

## Important: Old vs Modern Token Behavior

Older Kubernetes versions commonly created long-lived Secret objects associated with ServiceAccounts.

Modern Kubernetes generally uses short-lived projected tokens by default.

You should avoid creating long-lived ServiceAccount tokens unless there is a specific compatibility requirement.

The important security principle is:

```text
Use short-lived credentials whenever possible.
```

