# 20. Testing Permissions

One of the most useful RBAC commands is:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i
```

Check your current identity:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i get pods
```

Example output:

```text
yes
```

Check whether an action is allowed:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i delete pods
```

Example:

```text
no
```

## Test a ServiceAccount

For:

```text
Namespace: dev
ServiceAccount: app-sa
```

run:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i get pods \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:dev:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
yes
```

Test deletion:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i delete pods \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:dev:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
no
```

Test Deployments:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i create deployments \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:dev:app-sa
```

If the Role does not grant that permission:

```text
no
```

