# 24. Hands-on Lab

## Objective

Create a ServiceAccount that can:

```text
get Pods
list Pods
watch Pods
```

but cannot:

```text
delete Pods
create Deployments
```

---

## Step 1: Create namespace

```bash
kubectl create namespace rbac-demo
```

---

## Step 2: Create ServiceAccount

```bash
kubectl create serviceaccount app-sa \
  -n rbac-demo
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get sa -n rbac-demo
```

---

## Step 3: Create Role

Create `pod-reader.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: pod-reader
  namespace: rbac-demo

rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources:
      - pods
    verbs:
      - get
      - list
      - watch
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply -f pod-reader.yaml
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get role -n rbac-demo
```

---

## Step 4: Create RoleBinding

Create `rolebinding.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: app-sa-binding
  namespace: rbac-demo

subjects:
  - kind: ServiceAccount
    name: app-sa
    namespace: rbac-demo

roleRef:
  kind: Role
  name: pod-reader
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply -f rolebinding.yaml
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get rolebinding -n rbac-demo
```

---

## Step 5: Test allowed permission

```bash
kubectl auth can-i get pods \
  -n rbac-demo \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:rbac-demo:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
yes
```

Test:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i list pods \
  -n rbac-demo \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:rbac-demo:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
yes
```

Test:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i watch pods \
  -n rbac-demo \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:rbac-demo:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
yes
```

---

## Step 6: Test denied permissions

Try:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i delete pods \
  -n rbac-demo \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:rbac-demo:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
no
```

Try:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i create deployments \
  -n rbac-demo \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:rbac-demo:app-sa
```

Expected:

```text
no
```

---

## Step 7: Test namespace isolation

Try checking Pods in another namespace:

```bash
kubectl auth can-i get pods \
  -n default \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:rbac-demo:app-sa
```

The RoleBinding was created in `rbac-demo`, so the ServiceAccount should not receive the same namespaced Pod permissions in `default`.

This demonstrates an important RBAC concept:

```text
RBAC permissions
       +
Namespace
       =
Effective access
```

